<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Oyo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> was the reduced successor state of the Oyo Empire, founded further south after the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-ile">Oyo-Ile</a> was abandoned around 1835–1836. The dynasty continued to rule from the new centre. According to the site's Oyo Empire profile, it survived as a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> from 1888 until its final formal dissolution in 1896.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-oyo.jpg" alt="New Oyo" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tijani Lukman · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calabash_Carving.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
